From b0ddaf0acc7bb6b911d43fec5c8e348c7dd1cd82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Volker Lendecke <vl@samba.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lib: seed generate_unique_u64() per process again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since commit 89968416949 ("lib/util: make generate_unique_u64() more
robust") the first call in a process sets next_value to veto_value and
increments it before the veto check. So the random nonce is never
generated, and every process continues counting from the value it was
passed. Processes that start from the same value, for example the
unique_content_epoch of the same locking.tdb record, hand out the same
"unique" values. New g_lock records get unique_lock_epoch 1 and
unique_data_epoch 2 in every fresh process.

share_mode_memcache_fetch() relies on unique_content_epoch being unique
across processes to detect stale cached share_mode_data, g_lock relies
on unique_data_epoch to detect data changes for watchers. With
colliding epochs an smbd can use outdated share_mode_data or miss a
change of g_lock data.

Start every process at a random value as documented in samba_util.h.

BUG: https://bugzilla.samba.org/show_bug.cgi?id=16200

Signed-off-by: Volker Lendecke <vl@samba.org>
Reviewed-by: Stefan Metzmacher <metze@samba.org>

Autobuild-User(master): Volker Lendecke <vl@samba.org>
Autobuild-Date(master): Fri Oct  9 09:42:26 UTC 2026 on atb-devel-224

(cherry picked from commit 67eeb79811e57038a38d7272ee98064938b27b06)

Autobuild-User(v4-25-test): Björn Jacke <bjacke@samba.org>
Autobuild-Date(v4-25-test): Mon Oct 12 20:49:58 UTC 2026 on atb-devel-224
---
 lib/util/genrand_util.c                   | 9 ++++++++-
 selftest/knownfail.d/unique-content-epoch | 1 -
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 selftest/knownfail.d/unique-content-epoch

diff --git a/lib/util/genrand_util.c b/lib/util/genrand_util.c
index 193f5c0467fc..20a5e98d9af4 100644
--- a/lib/util/genrand_util.c
+++ b/lib/util/genrand_util.c
@@ -76,8 +76,15 @@ _PUBLIC_ uint64_t generate_unique_u64(uint64_t veto_value)
 	if (unlikely(pid != generate_unique_u64_state.pid)) {
 		generate_unique_u64_state = (struct generate_unique_u64_state) {
 			.pid = pid,
-			.next_value = veto_value,
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Start at a random value, processes must not
+		 * generate the same sequence of values.
+		 */
+		generate_nonce_buffer(
+			(void *)&generate_unique_u64_state.next_value,
+			sizeof(generate_unique_u64_state.next_value));
 	}
 
 	generate_unique_u64_state.next_value++;
diff --git a/selftest/knownfail.d/unique-content-epoch b/selftest/knownfail.d/unique-content-epoch
deleted file mode 100644
index 3bc80619ab9f..000000000000
--- a/selftest/knownfail.d/unique-content-epoch
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-^samba.tests.libsmb-basic.samba.tests.libsmb-basic.LibsmbTestCase.test_unique_content_epoch
